                ],
                [
                    "ttp",
                    [
                        [
                            "tactic",
                            "TA0001"
                        ],
                        [
                            "technique",
                            "T1566.001"
                        ]
                    ]
                ],
                [
                    "description",
                    "Mustang Panda leverages targeted spearphishing emails containing malicious attachments to gain initial access to victim environments. The group frequently disguises these attachments as legitimate documents related to government affairs, diplomatic communications, regional issues, or other topics relevant to the target. When opened, the attachments may execute malicious code, deploy malware, or initiate the download of additional payloads. Successful execution enables Mustang Panda to establish a foothold within the victim network, maintain persistence, and conduct espionage-focused operations."
                ],
